They cut the head, no. What about a nice hot glass of snake blood? But Japanese, they do drink snake blood. They do eat dog meat. It's a delicacy.

cue0146035
01:07:21.220 --> 01:07:34.300
Yes? Oh yes, they do. They do. But it's icky. It's icky what they do. Alright. Now, every culture has its taboos about food.

cue0146036
01:07:35.300 --> 01:07:45.020
We Americans have American taboos. Japanese, they don't have American taboos. They have the Japanese taboos. I don't know what they are, but I'm sure that they are.

cue0146037
01:07:45.020 --> 01:07:51.200
Yes? And there was three things, I don't know, there's a crazy people who eat cow.

cue0146038
01:07:53.700 --> 01:07:57.200
The Indians, for the Indians, if you eat cow, that is the worst thing ever.

cue0146039
01:07:58.160 --> 01:08:01.680
Every culture has its own taboos.

cue0146040
01:08:03.260 --> 01:08:06.380
You observe Kashrut, not Jewish Kashrut.

cue0146041
01:08:06.680 --> 01:08:07.700
That is my question.

cue0146042
01:08:08.040 --> 01:08:09.780
Why you want to observe American Kashrut?

cue0146043
01:08:09.820 --> 01:08:12.440
I'm not against observing American Kashrut, mind you.

cue0146044
01:08:12.440 --> 01:08:16.400
but also observe your own system of kashrut.

cue0146045
01:08:17.540 --> 01:08:19.460
Because when you say ichi,

cue0146046
01:08:20.780 --> 01:08:24.000
about dog meat,

cue0146047
01:08:25.400 --> 01:08:27.940
but pork, well, you know,

cue0146048
01:08:27.940 --> 01:08:32.360
means that you divested yourself

cue0146049
01:08:32.360 --> 01:08:36.780
from one of the most elementary things of a people,

cue0146050
01:08:36.980 --> 01:08:38.200
its own taboos.

cue0146051
01:08:38.200 --> 01:08:41.800
and you're adopting

cue0146052
01:08:41.800 --> 01:08:43.600
an alien taboo.

cue0146053
01:08:45.200 --> 01:08:45.980
I'm not saying

cue0146054
01:08:45.980 --> 01:08:47.840
you observe kashrut,

cue0146055
01:08:48.040 --> 01:08:49.620
but somebody else's kashrut.

cue0146056
01:08:50.080 --> 01:08:50.940
That is the point.

cue0146057
01:08:51.380 --> 01:08:52.360
That is what hurts.

cue0146058
01:08:53.300 --> 01:08:54.200
That is the sin.

cue0146059
01:08:55.160 --> 01:08:55.380
Alright?

cue0146060
01:08:55.560 --> 01:08:56.460
The sin is

cue0146061
01:08:56.460 --> 01:08:59.180
you observe

cue0146062
01:08:59.180 --> 01:09:01.740
only somebody else's taboos.

cue0146063
01:09:04.180 --> 01:09:05.100
Observe your own.

cue0146064
01:09:06.360 --> 01:09:06.760
So,

cue0146065
01:09:06.760 --> 01:09:09.360
that's the way to understand

cue0146066
01:09:09.360 --> 01:09:11.320
Judaism. They all, they have their own

cue0146067
01:09:11.320 --> 01:09:13.220
Tora Sheva Alpeh, and I respect

cue0146068
01:09:13.220 --> 01:09:14.700
other people's Tora Sheva Alpeh.

cue0146069
01:09:15.600 --> 01:09:17.320
What about our Tora Sheva Alpeh?

cue0146070
01:09:17.940 --> 01:09:19.260
You respect the Japanese

cue0146071
01:09:19.260 --> 01:09:20.400
tradition, it's fine.

cue0146072
01:09:21.380 --> 01:09:23.360
They have a right to a national memory.

cue0146073
01:09:23.620 --> 01:09:24.000
Right.

cue0146074
01:09:25.040 --> 01:09:27.060
What about our national memory?

cue0146075
01:09:28.160 --> 01:09:29.060
I remember,

cue0146076
01:09:29.300 --> 01:09:31.420
and I don't say this to criticize,

cue0146077
01:09:32.300 --> 01:09:32.440
but

cue0146078
01:09:32.440 --> 01:09:35.540
you know, in Israel,

cue0146079
01:09:35.540 --> 01:09:39.080
the secular Israeli is not like a secular American.

cue0146080
01:09:39.660 --> 01:09:40.720
Secular American is American.

cue0146081
01:09:41.100 --> 01:09:43.120
He's not religious, but he respects religion.

cue0146082
01:09:43.300 --> 01:09:44.040
He loves religion.

cue0146083
01:09:44.460 --> 01:09:49.620
Secular Israeli is somebody who respects religion,

cue0146084
01:09:49.780 --> 01:09:51.480
everybody's religion except the Jewish religion.

cue0146085
01:09:51.620 --> 01:09:52.480
It's anti-Jewish religion.

cue0146086
01:09:54.740 --> 01:09:58.440
And, you know, except the Jewish religion.

cue0146087
01:09:59.820 --> 01:10:01.660
I saw a fantastic thing in the program,

cue0146088
01:10:02.080 --> 01:10:03.320
and nobody caught it.

cue0146089
01:10:03.320 --> 01:10:13.820
one of the guys there, totally left wing, anti everything, and he's always talking against the rabbis,

cue0146090
01:10:13.820 --> 01:10:21.040
trying to impose their values on others, and then he comes and he protests,

cue0146091
01:10:21.220 --> 01:10:29.960
there are workers that come from Thailand, they come to Israel, and you know what they do?

cue0146092
01:10:29.960 --> 01:10:33.060
to eat dogs.

cue0146093
01:10:33.980 --> 01:10:36.860
And he wanted them to be prohibited.

cue0146094
01:10:37.380 --> 01:10:40.220
The most irrational thing to do in the world.

cue0146095
01:10:40.700 --> 01:10:42.060
To eat dogs.

cue0146096
01:10:44.140 --> 01:10:45.340
I have nothing against it.

cue0146097
01:10:46.040 --> 01:10:48.920
And we should not permit them to eat dogs.

cue0146098
01:10:50.120 --> 01:10:51.200
And he's talking about all this.

cue0146099
01:10:51.700 --> 01:10:52.300
And I would like to say,

cue0146100
01:10:52.540 --> 01:10:54.740
what about not eating pork?

cue0146101
01:10:54.740 --> 01:10:56.060
He would say, well, that is stupid.

cue0146102
01:10:56.600 --> 01:10:57.140
Why?

cue0146103
01:10:57.140 --> 01:11:05.780
because he accepts the goal taboo but doesn't accept the Jewish table got the

cue0146104
01:11:05.780 --> 01:11:15.080
point all right all right any other question you had a question

cue0146105
01:11:27.140 --> 01:11:32.860
Therefore, to me, to the word of God, or detract from it,

cue0146106
01:11:34.100 --> 01:11:38.140
like God says you shall kill a criminal who is convicted,

cue0146107
01:11:38.140 --> 01:11:41.100
and then you have a sanhedrin who says, no, you should not,

cue0146108
01:11:41.260 --> 01:11:43.420
even though it is said you are not going to do it.

cue0146109
01:11:44.420 --> 01:11:50.020
And then you see the diametrically opposed result to the extent of...

cue0146110
01:11:50.020 --> 01:11:51.320
I have a problem.

cue0146111
01:11:51.320 --> 01:11:55.000
First of all, hello?

cue0146112
01:11:56.040 --> 01:12:05.000
We disagree on many things, but you know that sometimes there is more affection about people who disagree than about people who agree.

cue0146113
01:12:05.420 --> 01:12:13.940
So I'm going to confess, when I came here today, I was hoping that he should be present.

cue0146114
01:12:14.420 --> 01:12:14.700
All right?

cue0146115
01:12:14.780 --> 01:12:16.660
I was hoping that he should be present.

cue0146116
01:12:16.660 --> 01:12:20.660
So I welcome the question, and I welcome the question because it's a good question.

cue0146117
01:12:20.660 --> 01:12:23.320
and it gives you opportunity to explain more.

cue0146118
01:12:26.140 --> 01:12:26.860
Lay mental.

cue0146119
01:12:29.160 --> 01:12:30.740
The Tora is the lay mental of Israel.

cue0146120
01:12:31.180 --> 01:12:31.840
The mental law.

cue0146121
01:12:32.420 --> 01:12:32.960
Listen to this.

cue0146122
01:12:35.140 --> 01:12:36.500
I, the first person,

cue0146123
01:12:37.360 --> 01:12:41.080
speaking to this wonderful lady, second person, all right?

cue0146124
01:12:41.720 --> 01:12:42.880
I say a word.

cue0146125
01:12:43.520 --> 01:12:45.280
I have something, a meaning in my head.

cue0146126
01:12:47.280 --> 01:12:49.640
But my word means nothing

cue0146127
01:12:49.640 --> 01:12:56.680
until she processed this word according to her mind.

cue0146128
01:12:58.700 --> 01:13:02.220
The meaning is not what I have in my mind,

cue0146129
01:13:02.220 --> 01:13:04.120
because once that I speak it,

cue0146130
01:13:04.600 --> 01:13:08.880
I address it, say to Mr. Ben-Harrosh,

cue0146131
01:13:09.880 --> 01:13:13.600
and now the meaning of the word is

cue0146132
01:13:13.600 --> 01:13:19.620
according to what the mind of Ben Arosh would process it.

cue0146133
01:13:20.380 --> 01:13:23.940
Now, if I instead of speaking to Mr. Ben Arosh,

cue0146134
01:13:24.000 --> 01:13:27.240
I would be talking to somebody from Finland

cue0146135
01:13:27.240 --> 01:13:30.240
with a different kind of background.

cue0146136
01:13:31.000 --> 01:13:32.700
He may take the same word

cue0146137
01:13:32.700 --> 01:13:36.420
and understand it differently

cue0146138
01:13:36.420 --> 01:13:38.020
because his mind is differently.

cue0146139
01:13:40.300 --> 01:13:42.360
God spoke the Tora

cue0146140
01:13:42.360 --> 01:13:46.180
not to the Aztecs.

cue0146141
01:13:46.500 --> 01:13:47.680
I'm talking about the homage.

cue0146142
01:13:48.040 --> 01:13:49.280
Maybe he gave another Tora to them.

cue0146143
01:13:49.540 --> 01:13:53.300
The homage, the message that God gave in Sinai.

cue0146144
01:13:54.440 --> 01:13:56.320
It was to us.

cue0146145
01:13:57.840 --> 01:14:03.140
And it depends on the way we, our mind, process this message.

cue0146146
01:14:04.480 --> 01:14:05.760
When God says,

cue0146147
01:14:05.760 --> 01:14:07.320
Ukshatam leotayadecha.

cue0146148
01:14:08.660 --> 01:14:11.060
For whatever reason, I don't care why.

cue0146149
01:14:11.060 --> 01:14:12.760
our mind processed this

cue0146150
01:14:12.760 --> 01:14:15.120
to Mr. Filin

cue0146151
01:14:15.120 --> 01:14:18.940
and that is the meaning of it

cue0146152
01:14:18.940 --> 01:14:21.140
because he spoke to us

cue0146153
01:14:21.140 --> 01:14:23.220
and that is the way

cue0146154
01:14:23.220 --> 01:14:24.620
we understood it

cue0146155
01:14:24.620 --> 01:14:26.960
and if we

cue0146156
01:14:26.960 --> 01:14:28.140
made a mistake

cue0146157
01:14:28.140 --> 01:14:30.900
nobody could tell us that he made a mistake

cue0146158
01:14:30.900 --> 01:14:33.860
because he didn't speak to Mr. A, B, C, D, E

cue0146159
01:14:33.860 --> 01:14:36.020
he spoke to us

cue0146160
01:14:36.020 --> 01:14:37.620
and that is the way

cue0146161
01:14:37.620 --> 01:14:39.080
we understood it

cue0146162
01:14:39.080 --> 01:14:47.580
And hasri shalom, if there is an error, then we pray to God, He knows our mind, He is the great communicator,

cue0146163
01:14:47.580 --> 01:14:56.080
He knows what terms to convey in order to deliver whatever message, He knows exactly our mind.

cue0146164
01:14:56.080 --> 01:15:01.580
So if He knew that uksharta amlota l'arecha, we are going to understand a tefillin,

cue0146165
01:15:01.580 --> 01:15:08.580
and instead of tefillin He wanted us to wear a bathing suit, He should have to choose a different term.

cue0146166
01:15:08.580 --> 01:15:14.660
He chose ukshatam leotarecha because he knew that for us ukshatam leotarecha means to put on tefillin.

cue0146167
01:15:16.100 --> 01:15:20.520
And therefore, by virtue of giving the Tora to us,

cue0146168
01:15:23.260 --> 01:15:26.500
the act of giving the Tora creates already Tora shebealpe.

cue0146169
01:15:26.760 --> 01:15:31.460
Once that you give the text, once that you issue this word out of your mouth,

cue0146170
01:15:32.480 --> 01:15:35.780
the word is no longer yours, it belongs to the second person.

cue0146171
01:15:35.780 --> 01:15:38.540
The way that second person understands it.

cue0146172
01:15:38.580 --> 01:15:41.360
and that is the meaning of the Tora

cue0146173
01:15:41.360 --> 01:15:44.280
you think that the text

cue0146174
01:15:44.280 --> 01:15:46.240
he didn't speak to you

cue0146175
01:15:46.240 --> 01:15:49.140
he spoke to the Jewish people

cue0146176
01:15:49.140 --> 01:15:52.160
Mr. Christian

cue0146177
01:15:52.160 --> 01:15:53.900
Mr. Buddhist

cue0146178
01:15:53.900 --> 01:15:54.920
Mr. Muslim

cue0146179
01:15:54.920 --> 01:15:57.060
he did not speak to you

cue0146180
01:15:57.060 --> 01:15:59.660
he spoke to us

cue0146181
01:15:59.660 --> 01:16:02.200
that is the way we understood it

cue0146182
01:16:02.200 --> 01:16:04.040
that is our lament time

cue0146183
01:16:04.040 --> 01:16:08.860
End of discussion

cue0146184
01:16:08.860 --> 01:16:10.300
The Tora says

cue0146185
01:16:10.300 --> 01:16:10.980
Zabachta

cue0146186
01:16:10.980 --> 01:16:12.040
slaughter

cue0146187
01:16:12.040 --> 01:16:17.180
How does it mean slaughter?

cue0146188
01:16:17.920 --> 01:16:18.660
We understand

cue0146189
01:16:18.660 --> 01:16:20.580
that it doesn't have to be a pegan

cue0146190
01:16:20.580 --> 01:16:22.400
that it will be slaughtered

cue0146191
01:16:22.400 --> 01:16:23.900
That is the way we understood it

cue0146192
01:16:23.900 --> 01:16:26.380
If God didn't want it

cue0146193
01:16:26.380 --> 01:16:28.040
us to understand this

cue0146194
01:16:28.040 --> 01:16:30.060
He should have chosen another word

cue0146195
01:16:30.060 --> 01:16:31.560
Yes

cue0146196
01:16:31.560 --> 01:16:33.720
Yes?

cue0146197
01:16:37.720 --> 01:16:40.860
Should I speak Spanish?

cue0146198
01:16:42.280 --> 01:16:43.320
Any other questions?

cue0146199
01:16:44.140 --> 01:16:45.380
Any other questions, ladies and gentlemen?

cue0146200
01:16:45.960 --> 01:16:46.900
I thank you.

cue0146201
01:16:47.700 --> 01:16:52.120
I thank you because you give me the opportunity to speak about subjects that I enjoy so much.

cue0146202
01:16:53.060 --> 01:16:55.740
And still I have some sort of fantasy.

cue0146203
01:16:55.740 --> 01:17:00.140
I tell you my fantasy with the permission of the Rabbi.

cue0146204
01:17:00.140 --> 01:17:01.840
I tell you what my fantasy is.

cue0146205
01:17:03.460 --> 01:17:07.540
I imagine some of you, yes,

cue0146206
01:17:08.880 --> 01:17:16.480
I imagine some of you asking Rami or Yaʿaqoḇ for a copy of this

cue0146207
01:17:16.480 --> 01:17:19.240
and taking it home and reading it.

cue0146208
01:17:19.740 --> 01:17:21.080
That is my fantasy.

cue0146209
01:17:21.680 --> 01:17:22.200
Anytime.

cue0146210
01:17:22.680 --> 01:17:23.400
Thank you very much.

cue0146211
